WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.730
Hi! A pizza is cut into 4 equal slices and you eat 1. How much did you eat? Today we'll learn fractions and compare them.

2
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:18.618
Cut a pizza into 4 equal parts. One part is one quarter, written 1/4.

3
00:00:18.768 --> 00:00:24.906
The bottom number is how many equal parts in all. The top number is how many we take.

4
00:00:25.056 --> 00:00:28.794
Every part of a fraction must be the same size.

5
00:00:28.944 --> 00:00:33.162
Four quarters make one whole pizza.

6
00:00:33.312 --> 00:00:39.450
With the same bottom number, compare the tops: 3/5 is bigger than 2/5.

7
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:45.930
When the tops are 1, a bigger bottom means smaller parts: 1/2 is bigger than 1/4.

8
00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.562
If you're not sure, draw two same-size shapes and compare.

9
00:00:50.712 --> 00:00:56.058
The more people share a cake, the less each person gets.

10
00:00:56.208 --> 00:01:01.626
Watch out! 4 is bigger than 2, but that doesn't make 1/4 bigger!

11
00:01:01.776 --> 00:01:06.474
Cutting into 4 parts gives smaller pieces than cutting into 2.

12
00:01:06.624 --> 00:01:11.178
So 1/4 is smaller than 1/2.

13
00:01:11.328 --> 00:01:22.914
Your turn! A shape is cut into 3 equal parts and 1 is shaded. What fraction is shaded? Pause and think.

14
00:01:23.064 --> 00:01:29.514
3 parts in all, 1 shaded: one third. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:29.664 --> 00:01:41.538
Another one! A cake is cut into 8 equal slices and 3 are eaten. What fraction is eaten? Pause and think.

16
00:01:41.688 --> 00:01:48.234
8 in all, 3 eaten: three eighths. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:48.384 --> 00:01:57.714
Here's another! Which is bigger, 3/5 or 4/5? Pause and think.

18
00:01:57.864 --> 00:02:05.538
Same bottom, and 4 is more than 3, so 4/5 is bigger. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:05.688 --> 00:02:14.730
Try one more! Which is bigger, 1/3 or 1/6? Pause and think.

20
00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:23.634
Both tops are 1. Thirds are bigger pieces than sixths, so 1/3 is bigger. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:23.784 --> 00:02:32.442
Try one more! Sixths: how many make one whole? Pause and think.

22
00:02:32.592 --> 00:02:37.962
Six sixths make one whole. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:38.112 --> 00:02:47.106
Last one! Which is greater, one third or one fifth? Pause and think.

24
00:02:47.256 --> 00:02:56.010
Both tops are 1; 3 parts are bigger than 5 parts, so one third is greater. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:08.394
Remember: fractions need equal parts. Bottom is the total, top is the parts taken. Same bottom, compare the tops. When tops are 1, the smaller bottom is bigger.

26
00:03:08.544 --> 00:03:13.842
When you cut fruit today, say what fraction each piece is!

